senses.gloss:
sīmābandha, m.,
(1) drawing a strict line of (moral) demarcation (between good and evil): ˚dhaḥ Mvy 〔6825〕; so Jap.; Tib. mtshams bcad pa; ˚dhaḥ kṛto bhavati (by Buddha, before he will enter nirvāṇa) Divy 〔150.21〕;
(2) drawing a (magic) boundary (‘magic circle’, Bendall and Rouse, Śikṣ 〔p. 136〕) as protection against evil: dṛṣṭyā manasā vā ˚dhaṃ karoti Śikṣ 〔139.10〕; ˚dhaṃ tataḥ kuryāt Suv 〔106.6〕, ˚dhaṃ samārabhet 7 (vss); similarly Māy 〔261.4〕; MSV 〔i.286.17〕.
